# Who must approve what.
#
# Ordinary application code is reviewed by your squad, which is the point of
# the programme. But a pull request can also edit the things that do the
# checking: the CI workflow, the secret scanner, the scorer, the thresholds.
# Branch protection on its own does not protect the checker from being edited
# by the thing it is checking.
#
# So these paths need approval from the programme operator. Everything else is
# yours. If you think one of these files is wrong, open the PR anyway and say
# why: several of them are wrong today because someone said so.

# The checks themselves
/.github/                       @gursohal
/.github/workflows/             @gursohal
/scripts/check-secrets.mjs      @gursohal
/scripts/doctor.mjs             @gursohal

# Scoring: the formulas, the harness, and anything that sets a pass mark
/src/scoring/                   @gursohal
/scripts/score.ts               @gursohal
/fixtures/                      @gursohal

# Rules people are held to
/docs/DATA-RULES.md             @gursohal
/docs/PREFLIGHT.md              @gursohal
/CLAUDE.md                      @gursohal

# Dependency and toolchain changes, because a build script is executable code
/package.json                   @gursohal
/pnpm-lock.yaml                 @gursohal
/pnpm-workspace.yaml            @gursohal
